INSERT INTO problems (slug,leetcode_id,title,description,difficulty,source_url,topics,companies,company_count,popularity,acceptance,recency,description_source,embedding) VALUES ('product-of-array-except-self',238,'Product of Array Except Self','Given an integer array nums , return an array answer such that answer[i] is equal to the product of all the elements of nums except nums[i] .

The product of any prefix or suffix of nums is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bit integer.

You must write an algorithm that runs in O(n) time and without using the division operation.

Example 1:

Input: nums = [1,2,3,4]
Output: [24,12,8,6]

Example 2:

Input: nums = [-1,1,0,-3,3]
Output: [0,0,9,0,0]

Constraints:

- 2 <= nums.length <= 10^5

- -30 <= nums[i] <= 30

- The input is generated such that answer[i] is guaranteed to fit in a 32-bit integer.

