INSERT INTO problems (slug,leetcode_id,title,description,difficulty,source_url,topics,companies,company_count,popularity,acceptance,recency,description_source,embedding) VALUES ('check-if-every-row-and-column-contains-all-numbers',2133,'Check if Every Row and Column Contains All Numbers','An n x n matrix is valid if every row and every column contains all the integers from 1 to n ( inclusive ).

Given an n x n integer matrix matrix , return true if the matrix is valid . Otherwise, return false .

Example 1:

Input: matrix = [[1,2,3],[3,1,2],[2,3,1]]
Output: true
Explanation: In this case, n = 3, and every row and column contains the numbers 1, 2, and 3.
Hence, we return true.

Example 2:

Input: matrix = [[1,1,1],[1,2,3],[1,2,3]]
Output: false
Explanation: In this case, n = 3, but the first row and the first column do not contain the numbers 2 or 3.
Hence, we return false.

Constraints:

- n == matrix.length == matrix[i].length

- 1 <= n <= 100

