INSERT INTO problems (slug,leetcode_id,title,description,difficulty,source_url,topics,companies,company_count,popularity,acceptance,recency,description_source,embedding) VALUES ('employee-importance',690,'Employee Importance','You have a data structure of employee information, including the employee''s unique ID, importance value, and direct subordinates'' IDs.

You are given an array of employees employees where:

- employees[i].id is the ID of the i^th employee.

- employees[i].importance is the importance value of the i^th employee.

- employees[i].subordinates is a list of the IDs of the direct subordinates of the i^th employee.

Given an integer id that represents an employee''s ID, return the total importance value of this employee and all their direct and indirect subordinates .

Example 1:

Input: employees = [[1,5,[2,3]],[2,3,[]],[3,3,[]]], id = 1
Output: 11
Explanation: Employee 1 has an importance value of 5 and has two direct subordinates: employee 2 and employee 3.
They both have an importance value of 3.
Thus, the total importance value of employee 1 is 5 + 3 + 3 = 11.

Example 2:

Input: employees = [[1,2,[5]],[5,-3,[]]], id = 5
Output: -3
Explanation: Employee 5 has an importance value of -3 and has no direct subordinates.
Thus, the total importance value of employee 5 is -3.

Constraints:

- 1 <= employees.length <= 2000

- 1 <= employees[i].id <= 2000

- All employees[i].id are unique .

- -100 <= employees[i].importance <= 100

- One employee has at most one direct leader and may have several subordinates.

- The IDs in employees[i].subordinates are valid IDs.','medium','https://leetcode.com/problems/employee-importance','{"Array","Hash Table","Tree","Depth-First Search","Breadth-First Search"}','{"amazon","bloomberg","google","microsoft","robinhood","uber"}',6,175.0,69.6,'3mo','leetcode','[-0.007380442, -0.015457802, 0.020738762, -0.083418034, -0.033406258, -0.014646635, -0.005141645, -0.009562661, 0.020400377, 0.010615916, -0.020034168, -0.0094789425, -0.013449527, 0.003115312, 0.13328683, -0.00045084176, 0.000941677, 0.013255164, 0.011408083, -0.02087157, -0.02998447, 0.0070261983, 0.016990187, -0.034416404, -0.02971747, -0.021855727, 0.015029543, 0.015569919, 0.015156472, -0.021030791, -0.008632888, 0.022166155, -0.0065934528, 0.03598581, 0.0077160033, -0.019220715, 1.04092205e-05, -0.016518436, -0.010010674, -0.025770197, 0.010592767, -0.0053297426, 0.010456138, -0.024729105, -0.019060351, -0.001200107, 0.0033052482, -0.022988757, -0.023252537, 0.017070593, 0.01171069, 0.027211763, -0.012184023, -0.19488765, -0.0011845407, -0.029980319, -0.0063636913, -0.025069926, -0.018130517, 0.010807103, 0.009088918, 0.024464712, -0.0012774415, 0.02180615, 0.0067216507, -0.014247731, 0.017928848, 0.0089255115, 0.019279791, 0.0020237004, 0.021201726, 0.011491505, -0.034581676, -0.018358096, -0.0035547465, -0.021543346, -0.016619803, -0.0143507505, 0.007498301, 0.021917777, -0.028110418, 0.0047789793, -0.015477652, -0.029165816, -0.010082537, 0.0062535508, -0.028962793, -0.014183394, 0.003652772, -0.01792102, 0.009848606, -0.003947948, 0.019411745, 0.015942607, -0.01999107, -0.014068088, 0.018945087, 0.0073168227, -0.0035527388, -0.018892692, -0.007999188, -0.03457349, -0.00033225943, 0.008129773, 0.007717477, -0.013016688, 0.036482804, 0.0012936643, 0.030700734, 0.0070153708, 0.013799946, -0.011179427, 0.022837711, -0.010169439, 0.015225256, -0.12544313, 0.011457721, 0.017043434, -0.003917904, -0.027812444, -0.026515964, 0.01169262, -0.014378382, -0.015025212, 0.015786014, -0.0